<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Service Cloud Voice org settings.

  `enableSCVExternalTelephony` is the flag behind "Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony"
  (a.k.a. BYOT / third-party telephony). Deploying this file is what turns Voice on; it is the
  metadata equivalent of the "Turn on Voice with Partner Telephony" toggle under step 2 of
  Setup / Salesforce Voice.

  VERIFIED on a fresh scratch org: the flag read false, `sf project deploy start` reported success,
  and a subsequent retrieve read true. No browser required. The setup script still verifies the
  result and can repair it through the UI, but that path is a fallback, not the normal route.

  `enableSCVBYOT` is the deprecated predecessor (API 52.0) and is deliberately not set here; setting
  both is contradictory.

  `enableServiceCloudVoice` is the *Amazon Connect* flag. It is intentionally left alone: turning it
  on drags in the Amazon Connect provisioning path (AWS account linkage, tax registration number,
  CloudFormation) that has nothing to do with a partner telephony package.

  PREREQUISITE, and the failure it causes:
  This deploy only means something in an org created with the ServiceCloudVoicePartnerTelephony,
  Scrt2Conversation and BYOOTT scratch org features. Without them the Setup page for Voice does not
  render at all, and Lightning's way of expressing that is not an error page but a permanent loading
  spinner with a "Sorry to interrupt / CSS Error" banner.

  NOTE ON XML COMMENTS: a double hyphen is illegal inside an XML comment, and the Metadata API
  rejects the whole file with "The string ... is not permitted within comments." Use = for rules and
  avoid double hyphens when editing this header.
-->
<ServiceCloudVoiceSettings xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <enableSCVExternalTelephony>true</enableSCVExternalTelephony>
</ServiceCloudVoiceSettings>
